{"term":"circumstance","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:101045e60d070ea7b6","definition":"Something which is related to, or in some way affects, a fact or event.","example":"The report should focus on to the current circumstances of the organisation, to help us find a way to grow in the future.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["circumstance","position","posture"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["aggravating circumstance","attendant circumstance","attenuating circumstance","exigent circumstance","extenuating circumstance","extenuating circumstances","mitigating circumstance","mitigating circumstances","pomp and circumstance","under no circumstance","under the circumstances"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circumstance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5a25610bf0b323c313","definition":"An event; a fact; a particular incident, occurrence, or condition (status).","example":"I have ſeen Two or Three antique Buſts of Alexander in the ſame Air and Poſture, and am apt to think the Sculptor had in his Thoughts the Conqueror's weeping for new Worlds, or ſome other the like Circumſtance of his History.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["circumstance","position","posture"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["aggravating circumstance","attendant circumstance","attenuating circumstance","exigent circumstance","extenuating circumstance","extenuating circumstances","mitigating circumstance","mitigating circumstances","pomp and circumstance","under no circumstance","under the circumstances"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circumstance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ce0970173639a1a705","definition":"Evasive or indirect language; circumlocution.","exa